cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Urban Wind Lab: An interactive lattice-Boltzmann tool for wind analysis"
abstract: >-
  Interactive lattice-Boltzmann wind analysis for 3D urban context, built for teaching
  architecture students. A D3Q19 lattice-Boltzmann solver with a Smagorinsky sub-grid model
  and an atmospheric boundary layer log-law inlet runs in the browser, reporting wind speed,
  amplification, pressure coefficient and Lawson pedestrian comfort classes. One
  self-contained HTML file with no build step and no dependencies.
authors:
